{{! cas-replace-composite-property: sketch section 4.3's
    CompositePropertyBoundary variant. There is no single graph to sweep:
    the closure is a bounded property-path walk over the composite
    property (a compile-time Mustache slot, the first composite property
    found by walking this target's boundary shape at compile time, see
    persistence.boundary and persistence.resolver). SPARQL 1.1 permits a
    property path only inside WHERE, never inside a DELETE or INSERT
    template block (a template's predicate position accepts a plain Verb
    only) -- this was caught by this template's own render-and-parse
    test, and is why the path below appears only in WHERE, binding
    ?member for the DELETE template to consume as a plain triple pattern.
    A property path also cannot itself be a SPARQL variable, and SPARQL
    1.1 property paths have no bounded repetition syntax, so depth is
    enforced at compile time by the shape walk's own cycle detection, not
    by a runtime bound here; the path below uses one-or-more repetition,
    matching the walked closure's reachability. The version row's subject
    is the root INSTANCE iri, never a graph iri (sketch section 4.3,
    point 1). The PAYLOAD marker below is a non-SPARQL text-substitution
    marker, not a bindable variable: a set of triples cannot be bound
    through a single SPARQL variable, so whatever executes this
    instantiated template must splice in the caller's already-serialised,
    trusted payload triples before submission -- see
    tools/persistence/README.md, Known limitations.

    Note for template authors: never put a Mustache tag inside this
    comment block, including inside prose describing a slot by name in
    braces. Chevron's comment parser ends at the first closing double-brace
    it sees, even one nested inside a triple-brace tag, which silently
    truncates the comment and corrupts everything after it. }}
PREFIX pat: <https://example.org/lattice/patterns#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

DELETE {
  ?root ?p1 ?o1 .
  ?member ?p2 ?o2 .
  GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} { $root pat:seq $expectedSeq ; pat:head ?prevRev }
}
INSERT {
  GRAPH ?logGraph { #PAYLOAD# }
  GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} { $root pat:epoch $epoch ; pat:seq $nextSeq ; pat:head $newRev }
  GRAPH {{{txnGraph}}}        { $txnId pat:rev $newRev }
  GRAPH ?logGraph2 {
      $newRev a pat:Revision ; pat:target $root ; pat:epoch $epoch ; pat:seq $nextSeq ;
              pat:prevRev ?prevRev ; pat:txn $txnId ; pat:recordedAt ?now
  }
}
WHERE {
  BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR({{{logGraphPrefix}}}), SUBSTR(STR(NOW()), 1, 7))) AS ?logGraph)
  BIND(?logGraph AS ?logGraph2)
  GRAPH {{{metaGraphPrefix}}} {
      $root pat:epoch $epoch ; pat:seq $expectedSeq ; pat:head ?prevRev
      FILTER NOT EXISTS { $root pat:deleted true }
  }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { GRAPH {{{txnGraph}}} { $txnId pat:rev ?any } }
  BIND(NOW() AS ?now)
  OPTIONAL { $root ?p1 ?o1 }
  OPTIONAL {
      $root {{{compositeProperty}}}+ ?member .
      ?member ?p2 ?o2
  }
}
